  "title": "Kourovka problem 11.95 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Suppose that G is a p-group G containing an element a of order p such that\nthe subgroup ⟨a, ag ⟩ is finite for any g and the set CG (a) ∩ aG is finite. Is it true that\nG has non-trivial centre? This is true for 2-groups.                         S. P. Strunkov",
